1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,548
Give hydrogen enough time,

2
00:00:01,798 --> 00:00:03,640
and it starts asking where it came from.

3
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,608
13.8 billion years ago,

4
00:00:06,608 --> 00:00:09,418
the Big Bang made hydrogen, a little helium,

5
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:11,250
and almost nothing else!

6
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,539
Then gravity went to work.

7
00:00:13,789 --> 00:00:14,857
It squeezed that gas

8
00:00:14,857 --> 00:00:16,940
until the first stars burst into light!

9
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:20,633
Inside them, hydrogen fused, step by step,

10
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:21,963
into carbon, oxygen,

11
00:00:22,213 --> 00:00:23,410
the atoms of life.

12
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:25,299
Those stars died,

13
00:00:25,299 --> 00:00:27,451
and blasted their atoms across space.

14
00:00:27,701 --> 00:00:29,620
New suns formed. Planets. Oceans.

15
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:30,993
And you?

16
00:00:31,293 --> 00:00:32,769
About 6 of every 10 atoms

17
00:00:32,769 --> 00:00:34,305
in your body are hydrogen,

18
00:00:34,605 --> 00:00:36,850
almost all of it made in the Big Bang.

19
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,056
You are that ancient gas,

20
00:00:39,056 --> 00:00:40,309
looking up at the stars.

21
00:00:40,709 --> 00:00:41,910
Which proves one thing.
